{"slug":"tom-foley","qid":"Q577751","name":"Tom Foley","desc":"American politician from Washington (1929–2013)","article":"Tom Foley","born":"1929-03-06","died":"2013-10-18","birthplace":"Spokane","parties":["Democratic Party"],"offices":[{"t":"United States Ambassador to Japan","w":"","f":1997,"u":2001},{"t":"Speaker of the House","w":"","f":1989,"u":1995},{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"WA-05","f":1965,"u":1995}],"summary":"Thomas Stephen Foley (March 6, 1929 – October 18, 2013) was an American lawyer, diplomat, and politician who served as the 49th speaker of the United States House of Representatives from 1989 to 1995. A member of the Democratic Party, Foley represented Washington's 5th congressional district for 30 years (1965–1995). He was the first speaker of the House in over a century since Galusha Grow in 1862 to be defeated in a re-election campaign.","photo":null,"history":[{"y":1994,"o":"H","k":"WA-05","p":"D","v":106074,"s":49.08,"w":false,"n":"Thomas S Foley"},{"y":1992,"o":"H","k":"WA-05","p":"D","v":135965,"s":55.18,"w":true,"n":"Thomas S Foley"},{"y":1990,"o":"H","k":"WA-05","p":"D","v":110234,"s":68.81,"w":true,"n":"Thomas S Foley"},{"y":1988,"o":"H","k":"WA-05","p":"D","v":160654,"s":76.39,"w":true,"n":"Thomas S Foley"},{"y":1986,"o":"H","k":"WA-05","p":"D","v":121732,"s":74.72,"w":true,"n":"Thomas S Foley"},{"y":1984,"o":"H","k":"WA-05","p":"D","v":154988,"s":69.68,"w":true,"n":"Thomas S Foley"},{"y":1982,"o":"H","k":"WA-05","p":"D","v":109549,"s":64.3,"w":true,"n":"Thomas S Foley"},{"y":1980,"o":"H","k":"WA-05","p":"D","v":120530,"s":51.9,"w":true,"n":"Thomas S Foley"},{"y":1978,"o":"H","k":"WA-05","p":"D","v":77201,"s":48.0,"w":true,"n":"Thomas S Foley"},{"y":1976,"o":"H","k":"WA-05","p":"D","v":120415,"s":58.01,"w":true,"n":"Thomas S Foley"}]}